msgstr "Albata^F"

msgid "DLC@SECRETSOFTHEARCHMAGES@LORDS@ALBATA@SECONDNAME"
msgstr "Firebeak^z"

msgid "DLC@SECRETSOFTHEARCHMAGES@LORDS@ALBATA@TITLE"
msgstr "Matron"

msgid "DLC@SECRETSOFTHEARCHMAGES@LORDS@ALBATA@TITLE@GENDER"
msgstr "^f"

msgid "DLC@SECRETSOFTHEARCHMAGES@LORDS@ALBATA_CITY@NAME"
msgstr "Ashbarn^N"

msgid "DLC@SECRETSOFTHEARCHMAGES@LORDS@ALBATA_CITY@NAME_2"
msgstr "Parlimenth^N"

msgid "DLC@SECRETSOFTHEARCHMAGES@LORDS@ALBATA_CITY@NAME_3"
msgstr "Blazecamp^N"

msgid "DLC@SECRETSOFTHEARCHMAGES@LORDS@ALBATA_RACE@BIO"
msgstr "Used as payment for an infernal pact, Albata and the Redfeathers were cast into the depths of the Azh'Ruun Pit. But the Demons had bitten off more than they could chew. The Matron and her tribe escaped their imprisonment and learned the ways of the Fiends, feasting upon them and fleeing the infernal realm.[br/][br/]In their Demonic odyssey, the Redfeathers lost their connection with their [hyperlink,GLOBAL.PrimalSpiritsLoreConcept]Primal Spirit[/hyperlink]. Yet in {GLOBAL.ObbadothLoreConcept.Hyperlink}, they forged a bond with the Inferno Hounds, which became their animal guide. Now the barbarian tribe and its leader seek the one responsible for their sacrifice, even if they have to go back to hell to find answers."

msgid "DLC@SECRETSOFTHEARCHMAGES@LORDS@ALBATA_RACE@NAME"
msgstr "Redfeathers"

msgid "DLC@SECRETSOFTHEARCHMAGES@LORDS@ARACHNA_RACE@BIO"
msgstr "Ever close-lipped and withdrawn, Arachna kept her double role as member of the [hyperlink,GLOBAL.CircleOfDeogaiLoreConcept]Circles[/hyperlink] of Evermore and Witherbloom a secret throughout the Ages. Only now, as the Mistwalkers invade the {GLOBAL.WorldsWithinLoreConcept.Hyperlink} more openly, rumors of her allegiance with the {GLOBAL.DuathadaeLoreConcept.Hyperlink} are beginning to spread. When Arachna weaves her cold webs and enchantments, Onoka, the Queen of Whispers, shows her eerie smile.[br/][br/]The Weaving Mistcrawlers are relatives of the Spider Queen herself, distant descendants of the turned Raven Tharic and his Mistwalkers. With them by her side, Arachna has spent ages weaving schemes, ensnaring first Athla and then all {GLOBAL.MagehavenLoreConcept.Hyperlink} in her web of lies."

msgid "DLC@SECRETSOFTHEARCHMAGES@LORDS@ARACHNA_RACE@NAME"
msgstr "Weaving Mistcrawlers"

msgid "DLC@SECRETSOFTHEARCHMAGES@LORDS@DADAYO@NAME"
msgstr "DaDa Yuah^F"

msgid "DLC@SECRETSOFTHEARCHMAGES@LORDS@DADAYO@SECONDNAME"
msgstr "Demonic Princess of Attrition^z"

msgid "DLC@SECRETSOFTHEARCHMAGES@LORDS@DADAYO@TITLE"
msgstr "Top Dog"

msgid "DLC@SECRETSOFTHEARCHMAGES@LORDS@DADAYO@TITLE@GENDER"
msgstr "^f"

msgid "DLC@SECRETSOFTHEARCHMAGES@LORDS@DADAYO_CITY_NAME"
msgstr "The Chain of Impatience^N"

msgid "DLC@SECRETSOFTHEARCHMAGES@LORDS@DADAYO_CITY_NAME_00"
msgstr "Temple of Unending Toils^N"

msgid "DLC@SECRETSOFTHEARCHMAGES@LORDS@DADAYO_CITY_NAME_01"
msgstr "Urgent Stairways^N"

msgid "DLC@SECRETSOFTHEARCHMAGES@LORDS@DADAYO_CITY_NAME_02"
msgstr "Imprudent Crossroad^N"

msgid "DLC@SECRETSOFTHEARCHMAGES@LORDS@DADAYO_CITY_NAME_03"
msgstr "Reckless Kennels^N"

msgid "DLC@SECRETSOFTHEARCHMAGES@LORDS@DADAYO_RAC@NAME"
msgstr "Bolting Houndmasters"

msgid "DLC@SECRETSOFTHEARCHMAGES@LORDS@DADAYO_RACE@BIO"
msgstr "At the gleeful crack of her whip, DaDa Yuah commands urgency and impatience in the hearts of mortals. To get stuff done, to reach greater speeds, or simply lose oneself to existential anxiety. Once that fear is allowed to fester, she inevitably becomes the angry little devil on their heels. [br/][br/]Before her, dash the Bolting Houndmasters, hunters of laggardly spirits and all those who eventually tarry before the infernal whip of impatience. They are the rabid and restless servants of the [hyperlink,GLOBAL.DemonicOverlordLoreConcept]Harridanmother[/hyperlink], and they must not, and cannot sit idle."

msgid "DLC@SECRETSOFTHEARCHMAGES@LORDS@DISCIPLE_SPRING@NAME"
msgstr "Lobelia^F"

msgid "DLC@SECRETSOFTHEARCHMAGES@LORDS@DISCIPLE_SPRING@RACE"
msgstr "Skittish Pellari"

msgid "DLC@SECRETSOFTHEARCHMAGES@LORDS@DISCIPLE_SPRING@SECONDNAME"
msgstr "Greyfang^z"

msgid "DLC@SECRETSOFTHEARCHMAGES@LORDS@DISCIPLE_SPRING@TITLE"
msgstr "Howlwarden"

msgid "DLC@SECRETSOFTHEARCHMAGES@LORDS@DISCIPLE_SPRING@TITLE@GENDER"
msgstr "^f"

msgid "DLC@SECRETSOFTHEARCHMAGES@LORDS@DISCIPLE_SPRING_CITY@NAME"
msgstr "Wools' End"

msgid "DLC@SECRETSOFTHEARCHMAGES@LORDS@DISCIPLE_SPRING_RACE@BIO"
msgstr "The Disciple of Ilandra has taken upon herself to defend the {GLOBAL.PellariLoreConcept.Hyperlink}, becoming a paragon among her kind. For it is rare to see one of the animalistic folk of {GLOBAL.DuathaLoreConcept.Hyperlink} ascend to Godirhood. As a native of the realm, Auntie Lobelia enjoys the favor of the {GLOBAL.DuathadaeLoreConcept.Hyperlink}, who regard her actions with far greater benevolence—at least compared to the other disciples in the Circle of Witherbloom. [br/][br/]The ancient tongues tell that the Skittish Pellari were already there when the Fey first came into being. And when the latter took control and became the favorites of Duatha, the fearful hares endured by retreating deep into the Burrow Downs. To them, fear is not cowardice, but survival."

msgid "DLC@SECRETSOFTHEARCHMAGES@LORDS@DISCIPLE_SUMMER@NAME"
msgstr "Kana-Grump^P"

msgid "DLC@SECRETSOFTHEARCHMAGES@LORDS@DISCIPLE_SUMMER@SECONDNAME"
msgstr "the Twineater^z"

msgid "DLC@SECRETSOFTHEARCHMAGES@LORDS@DISCIPLE_SUMMER@TITLE"
msgstr "Gargantumaw"

msgid "DLC@SECRETSOFTHEARCHMAGES@LORDS@DISCIPLE_SUMMER@TITLE@GENDER"
msgstr "^p"

msgid "DLC@SECRETSOFTHEARCHMAGES@LORDS@DISCIPLE_SUMMER_CITY@NAME"
msgstr "Paunch^N"

msgid "DLC@SECRETSOFTHEARCHMAGES@LORDS@DISCIPLE_SUMMER_RACE@BIO"
msgstr "Kana and Grump were once two chieftains of the Blood Clan, distant, degenerate descendants of [hyperlink,GLOBAL.MyrridaLoreConcept]Myrrida's[/hyperlink]mighty[hyperlink,GLOBAL.GiantKingLoreConcept]Giant Kings[/hyperlink]. In a feud, the two rival tribes fought each other to extinction. Only Grump survived; he devoured the body of Kana and grafted her head onto himself in the delirium of battle. Thus, they became one, the Twineater. [br/][br/]Lured to {GLOBAL.DuathaLoreConcept.Hyperlink}, Kana-Grump became the Disciple of Ventrogh in the Circle of Witherbloom, leading the Voracious Vermin. Those known to be the most ravenous inhabitants of the realm, insatiable creatures willing to devour even themselves under the orders of their gluttonous master. The rodent pest have eagerly taken up the task of hunting rebels beneath Duatha's surface. A place they call, in hungry whispers, Marrow Downs."

msgid "DLC@SECRETSOFTHEARCHMAGES@LORDS@DISCIPLE_SUMMER_RACE@NAME"
msgstr "Voracious Vermin"

msgid "DLC@SECRETSOFTHEARCHMAGES@LORDS@HAM@TITLE"
msgstr "Burrow-Warden"

msgid "DLC@SECRETSOFTHEARCHMAGES@LORDS@HAM@TITLE@GENDER"
msgstr "^m"

msgid "DLC@SECRETSOFTHEARCHMAGES@LORDS@HAM_CITY@NAME"
msgstr "Lollburrow^N"

msgid "DLC@SECRETSOFTHEARCHMAGES@LORDS@HAM_RACE@BIO"
msgstr "Bound and taken captive, our jovial Ham Binger was brought before the {GLOBAL.DuathadaeLoreConcept.Hyperlink}. But just before he was devoured, a strange Fey magic whisked him away... once again. In his defense, this time not even he knows how it happened. Yet now he has become the Chosen of the Fey and the leader of the Burrow Downs rebellion. [br/][br/]The Burrowing Pellari welcomed Ham with open paws. Changed by Fey magic, he has fully embraced life among the {GLOBAL.PellariLoreConcept.Hyperlink}. It has been a long time since the Burrow Warden has felt like he belongs. And so, his days of running are over; it is time to defend his home."

msgid "DLC@SECRETSOFTHEARCHMAGES@LORDS@HAM_RACE@NAME"
msgstr "Burrowing Pellari"

msgid "DLC@SECRETSOFTHEARCHMAGES@LORDS@ISTARNECH@NAME\t"
msgstr "Istarnech^M"

msgid "DLC@SECRETSOFTHEARCHMAGES@LORDS@ISTARNECH@SECONDNAME"
msgstr "Gold-Curser^z"

msgid "DLC@SECRETSOFTHEARCHMAGES@LORDS@ISTARNECH@TITLE"
msgstr "Traitor King"

msgid "DLC@SECRETSOFTHEARCHMAGES@LORDS@ISTARNECH@TITLE@GENDER"
msgstr "^m"

msgid "DLC@SECRETSOFTHEARCHMAGES@LORDS@ISTARNECH_CITY_NAME"
msgstr "The Chain of Greed^N"

msgid "DLC@SECRETSOFTHEARCHMAGES@LORDS@ISTARNECH_CITY_NAME_00"
msgstr "Kingdom of Want^N"

msgid "DLC@SECRETSOFTHEARCHMAGES@LORDS@ISTARNECH_CITY_NAME_01"
msgstr "Everbarren Hoard^N"

msgid "DLC@SECRETSOFTHEARCHMAGES@LORDS@ISTARNECH_CITY_NAME_02"
msgstr "Miserly Warrens^N"

msgid "DLC@SECRETSOFTHEARCHMAGES@LORDS@ISTARNECH_CITY_NAME_03"
msgstr "Penurious Pridevault^N"

msgid "DLC@SECRETSOFTHEARCHMAGES@LORDS@ISTARNECH_RAC@NAME"
msgstr "Avaricious Wolves"

msgid "DLC@SECRETSOFTHEARCHMAGES@LORDS@ISTARNECH_RACE@BIO"
msgstr "One of the last living {GLOBAL.TraitorKingsLoreConcept.Hyperlink} of old {GLOBAL.MyrridaLoreConcept.Hyperlink}. Istarnech Gold-Curser, he who denied the {GLOBAL.AllfatherLoreConcept.Hyperlink} before his peers and ate several treasures of the {GLOBAL.EternalCouncilLoreConcept.Hyperlink}. For this, he was chased out and down before finding shelter in eternal devotion to \"the Need.\" [br/][br/]The Avaricious Wolves are a terribly greedy bunch. All are born in servitude to the Demon Overlord of Avarice, thus their loyalty lies not so much with Istarnech, but rather with the giant hole in his stomach that litters all the treasures he eats across the floor."

msgid "DLC@SECRETSOFTHEARCHMAGES@LORDS@KARISSA@NAME"
msgstr "Karissa^F"

msgid "DLC@SECRETSOFTHEARCHMAGES@LORDS@KARISSA@SECONDNAME"
msgstr "the Fury^z"

msgid "DLC@SECRETSOFTHEARCHMAGES@LORDS@KARISSA@TITLE"
msgstr "Aspect of Chaos"

msgid "DLC@SECRETSOFTHEARCHMAGES@LORDS@KARISSA@TITLE@GENDER"
msgstr "^f"

msgid "DLC@SECRETSOFTHEARCHMAGES@LORDS@KARISSA_CITY_NAME"
msgstr "Raging Pyre^N"

msgid "DLC@SECRETSOFTHEARCHMAGES@LORDS@KARISSA_CITY_NAME_01"
msgstr "Rapture's Kindle^N"

msgid "DLC@SECRETSOFTHEARCHMAGES@LORDS@KARISSA_CITY_NAME_02"
msgstr "Manic Crucible^N"

msgid "DLC@SECRETSOFTHEARCHMAGES@LORDS@KARISSA_CITY_NAME_03"
msgstr "Heartfire Revels^N"

msgid "DLC@SECRETSOFTHEARCHMAGES@LORDS@KARISSA_RACE@BIO"
msgstr "Perisher of weaker hearts and prime Aspect of Chaos: Karissa—formerly \"the Red\"—whose dormant, primal being has been liberated by the [hyperlink,GLOBAL.EndailonLoreConcept]Chaos Endailon[/hyperlink]. Now, she is reborn as \"the Fury,\" harbinger of change, undoer of order, and the indomitable spark destined to set the {GLOBAL.WorldsWithinLoreConcept.Hyperlink} ablaze—one heart at a time. Through her, Chaos shall reign completely across the {GLOBAL.AstralSeaLoreConcept.Hyperlink}, and the old order shall be buried under her raging heels. And a new one shall arise from its ashes, one where all shall praise her. Praise her and rage on! [br/][br/]The Enchanted Chaotes are but savage animals in the eyes of orderly mortals, but they care nothing for such idle judgments. For they are the followers of Karissa and her very weapons of undoing, before whom all shall ultimately perish. \"For Chaos! For Karissa!\" they shout in their rampant march, \"Our One and Only Mistress!\" And they are marching for your gates."

msgid "DLC@SECRETSOFTHEARCHMAGES@LORDS@KARISSA_RACE@NAME"
msgstr "Enchanted Chaotes"

msgid "DLC@SECRETSOFTHEARCHMAGES@LORDS@MERLIN@TITLE"
msgstr "Grand Abdicator"

msgid "DLC@SECRETSOFTHEARCHMAGES@LORDS@MERLIN@TITLE@GENDER"
msgstr "^m"

msgid "DLC@SECRETSOFTHEARCHMAGES@LORDS@MERLIN_CITY@NAME"
msgstr "Memento^N"

msgid "DLC@SECRETSOFTHEARCHMAGES@LORDS@MERLIN_RACE@BIO"
msgstr "After attacking the {GLOBAL.WorldsWithinLoreConcept.Hyperlink} as an {GLOBAL.EldritchSovereignLoreConcept.Hyperlink} in the {GLOBAL.GreatUmbralWarLoreConcept.Hyperlink}, Merlin was at last freed from [hyperlink,GLOBAL.UrrathLoreConcept]Urrath's[/hyperlink] grasp on the Cliffs of Sordünn. Now the voices are gone, but not the guilt. Unable to trust himself, the Tarnished Archmage has covered his body with spells, wards, and amulets, going so far as to inscribe them into his own flesh. Damping his magic powers for the safety of those he swore to protect.[br/][br/]The {GLOBAL.HorwyndLoreConcept.Hyperlink} are an ancient and secretive people. When the {GLOBAL.CircleOfDeogaiLoreConcept.Hyperlink} were formed in ages past, the Horwynd devised the Shrouded Isles to undermine Archon supremacy. Though they only insinuate their motives for doing so or for seeking out Merlin at this point of time."

msgid "DLC@SECRETSOFTHEARCHMAGES@LORDS@MERLIN_RACE@NAME"
msgstr "Horwynd"

msgid "DLC@SECRETSOFTHEARCHMAGES@LORDS@NEKRON@SECONDNAME"
msgstr "Almighty^z"

msgid "DLC@SECRETSOFTHEARCHMAGES@LORDS@NEKRON@TITLE"
msgstr "Archreaper"

msgid "DLC@SECRETSOFTHEARCHMAGES@LORDS@NEKRON@TITLE@GENDER"
msgstr "^m"

msgid "DLC@SECRETSOFTHEARCHMAGES@LORDS@NEKRON_CITY@NAME"
msgstr "Risen^N"

msgid "DLC@SECRETSOFTHEARCHMAGES@LORDS@NEKRON_RACE@BIO"
msgstr "As life evolves in the {GLOBAL.WorldsWithinLoreConcept.Hyperlink}, so too does death. Nekron has ascended into a new and even [hyperlink,GLOBAL.EldritchSovereignLoreConcept]more corrupted form[/hyperlink], with the power of {GLOBAL.UrrathLoreConcept.Hyperlink} coursing through his necrotic body. The Archreaper now masters every domain of undead magic, and he intends to spread them to bring an Age of Death to the entire {GLOBAL.AstralSeaLoreConcept.Hyperlink}.[br/][br/]After the seals on {GLOBAL.AthlaLoreConcept.Hyperlink} were broken, Nekron did not join the invasion of the {GLOBAL.ShadraiFactionLoreConcept.Hyperlink}. Instead, he waited until he could return to Evermore unnoticed. There, he has been raising the Evermore Wights, lingering souls of the elves who once sought their last peace beyond Athla."

msgid "DLC@SECRETSOFTHEARCHMAGES@LORDS@NEKRON_RACE@NAME"
msgstr "Evermore Wights"

msgid "DLC@SECRETSOFTHEARCHMAGES@LORDS@PALAS@NAME"
msgstr "Palas^M"

msgid "DLC@SECRETSOFTHEARCHMAGES@LORDS@PALAS@SECONDNAME"
msgstr "Howling^z"

msgid "DLC@SECRETSOFTHEARCHMAGES@LORDS@PALAS@TITLE"
msgstr "Master Archivist"

msgid "DLC@SECRETSOFTHEARCHMAGES@LORDS@PALAS@TITLE@GENDER"
msgstr "^m"

msgid "DLC@SECRETSOFTHEARCHMAGES@LORDS@PALAS_CITY@NAME"
msgstr "Great Library of Xandrias^N"

msgid "DLC@SECRETSOFTHEARCHMAGES@LORDS@PALAS_CITY@NAME_2"
msgstr "Doom Archive^N"

msgid "DLC@SECRETSOFTHEARCHMAGES@LORDS@PALAS_CITY@NAME_3"
msgstr "Lore Vault^N"

msgid "DLC@SECRETSOFTHEARCHMAGES@LORDS@PALAS_RACE@BIO"
msgstr "At his young age, Palas had already achieved the rank of Master Archivist, guarding the knowledge and secrets of the Great Library of Xandrias. Yet his curiosity led him to read a grimoire from the forbidden section, which cursed his eyes, nearly shattered his sanity, and unleashed dark powers within his library. [br/][br/]The Cryptic Archivists were once part of the {GLOBAL.SchoolOfShroudingLoreConcept.Hyperlink}. But obsessed by lost magic, they drifted away from the {GLOBAL.HorwyndLoreConcept.Hyperlink}. Now Palas and the laconic librarians look for a master. Someone capable of teaching them how to keep the dark secrets of the library under control."

msgid "DLC@SECRETSOFTHEARCHMAGES@LORDS@PALAS_RACE@NAME"
msgstr "Cryptic Archivists"

msgid "DLC@SECRETSOFTHEARCHMAGES@LORDS@RESKAR@NAME"
msgstr "Reskar^M"

msgid "DLC@SECRETSOFTHEARCHMAGES@LORDS@RESKAR@SECONDNAME"
msgstr "Scapeshaper^z"

msgid "DLC@SECRETSOFTHEARCHMAGES@LORDS@RESKAR@TITLE"
msgstr "Emissary"

msgid "DLC@SECRETSOFTHEARCHMAGES@LORDS@RESKAR@TITLE@GENDER"
msgstr "^m"

msgid "DLC@SECRETSOFTHEARCHMAGES@LORDS@RESKAR_CITY@NAME"
msgstr "Grovetender's Gift^Ng"

msgid "DLC@SECRETSOFTHEARCHMAGES@LORDS@RESKAR_RACE@BIO"
msgstr "After the military campaigns of the Third Age, Reskar Scapeshaper continued his efforts to restore the blessing of the [hyperlink,GLOBAL.DragonsLoreConcept]Dragons[/hyperlink] to his kin. Uniting many Draconians under the same banner, Reskar's quest received new meaning when the Elder Dragon Sumuskira the Grovetender visited him after Lithyl's thwarted invasion of Athla.[br/][br/]Guided by visions from the Primal Dragon of Nature, the Rootseeker Draconians and their Emissary have embarked upon a new journey to reclaim the lost legacy of their ancestors—a legacy that predates even the First Age of Wonders."

msgid "DLC@SECRETSOFTHEARCHMAGES@LORDS@RESKAR_RACE@NAME"
msgstr "Rootseeker Draconians"

msgid "DLC@SECRETSOFTHEARCHMAGES@LORDS@SOARIN@NAME"
msgstr "Soarin^M"

msgid "DLC@SECRETSOFTHEARCHMAGES@LORDS@SOARIN@SECONDNAME"
msgstr "Boltwing^z"

msgid "DLC@SECRETSOFTHEARCHMAGES@LORDS@SOARIN@TITLE"
msgstr "Vindicator"

msgid "DLC@SECRETSOFTHEARCHMAGES@LORDS@SOARIN@TITLE@GENDER"
msgstr "^m"

msgid "DLC@SECRETSOFTHEARCHMAGES@LORDS@SOARIN_CITY@NAME"
msgstr "Airloom^N"

msgid "DLC@SECRETSOFTHEARCHMAGES@LORDS@SOARIN_RACE@BIO"
msgstr "Distant descendants of the {GLOBAL.HorwyndLoreConcept.Hyperlink}, the ancestors of Soaring Boltwing lived for generations alongside the Dwarves of an exiled realm. Yet the pride of the Vindicator chafed against the restraints and limitations imposed by those he deemed inferior, mere \"cave-dwellers.\" And so, he led his people away, seeking a place where his kind would be granted the honor they deserved. [br/][br/]The Skyshatter Fowl arrived in {GLOBAL.DuathaLoreConcept.Hyperlink} with their leader, who became the Disciple of Luth in the Circle of Witherbloom. In his wake, they claimed what they saw as their rightful place, hunting those who dwell beneath the surface. A fitting twist of fate, one that surely amuses the proud birds."

msgid "DLC@SECRETSOFTHEARCHMAGES@LORDS@SOARIN_RACE@NAME"
msgstr "Skyshatter Fowl"

msgid "DLC@SECRETSOFTHEARCHMAGES@LORDS@SYMON"
msgstr "Symon^M"

msgid "DLC@SECRETSOFTHEARCHMAGES@LORDS@SYMON@BIO"
msgstr "Exiled as a child with dangerous magic abilities, Symon learned the hard way what it means to be different. When the wizards of Evermore had left {GLOBAL.AthlaLoreConcept.Hyperlink} in pursuit of the [hyperlink,GLOBAL.ShadowDemonsLoreConcept]Shadow Demons[/hyperlink], Symon followed his sensitive arcane instincts to Evermore, where he found an Eldritch Leviathan waking up beneath the island. With great presence of mind Symon enchanted the Leviathan back into sleep, keeping solitary vigil while Athla became locked from Evermore through the seals of the Third Age. During this time Symon studied the cosmic secrets left behind by the [hyperlink,GLOBAL.CircleOfDeogaiLoreConcept]Circle[/hyperlink], but over time the endless struggle with the Leviathan and its desire to break free have taken their toll.[br/][br/]The Flowborn Halflings are a reflection of Symon's solitude, phantom images created to fight against the isolation and sorrow of being forgotten. They are a masterwork of illusion, almost a perfect remembrance of that distant memory when he was happy."

msgid "DLC@SECRETSOFTHEARCHMAGES@LORDS@SYMON@TITLE"
msgstr "Awakener"

msgid "DLC@SECRETSOFTHEARCHMAGES@LORDS@SYMON@TITLE@GENDER"
msgstr "^m"

msgid "DLC@SECRETSOFTHEARCHMAGES@LORDS@SYMON_CITY@NAME"
msgstr "Merryment^N"

msgid "DLC@SECRETSOFTHEARCHMAGES@LORDS@SYMON_MASKED"
msgstr "Mysterious Mage^M"

msgid "DLC@SECRETSOFTHEARCHMAGES@LORDS@SYMON_MASKED@BIO"
msgstr "Calling himself a Cosmic Wanderer, the mysterious mage keeps his identity concealed. He claims to have come to Evermore in search of the [hyperlink,GLOBAL.EndailonLoreConcept]Astral Endailon[/hyperlink], but his true motives remain a mystery."

msgid "DLC@SECRETSOFTHEARCHMAGES@LORDS@SYMON_RACE@NAME"
msgstr "Flowborn Halflings"

msgid "DLC@SECRETSOFTHEARCHMAGES@LORDS@WALBURGIS@NAME"
msgstr "Walburgis^M"

msgid "DLC@SECRETSOFTHEARCHMAGES@LORDS@WALBURGIS@SECONDNAME"
msgstr "Demonic Prince of Darkness^z"

msgid "DLC@SECRETSOFTHEARCHMAGES@LORDS@WALBURGIS@TITLE"
msgstr "Antisaint"

msgid "DLC@SECRETSOFTHEARCHMAGES@LORDS@WALBURGIS@TITLE@GENDER"
msgstr "^m"

msgid "DLC@SECRETSOFTHEARCHMAGES@LORDS@WALBURGIS_CITY_NAME"
msgstr "The Chain of Anguish^N"

msgid "DLC@SECRETSOFTHEARCHMAGES@LORDS@WALBURGIS_CITY_NAME_00"
msgstr "Bloodgurgler Gates^N"

msgid "DLC@SECRETSOFTHEARCHMAGES@LORDS@WALBURGIS_CITY_NAME_01"
msgstr "Altar of Darkness^N"

msgid "DLC@SECRETSOFTHEARCHMAGES@LORDS@WALBURGIS_CITY_NAME_02"
msgstr "Antisanctorium^N"

msgid "DLC@SECRETSOFTHEARCHMAGES@LORDS@WALBURGIS_CITY_NAME_03"
msgstr "Woeful Wallows^N"

msgid "DLC@SECRETSOFTHEARCHMAGES@LORDS@WALBURGIS_RAC@NAME"
msgstr "Bloodgurgler Legion"

msgid "DLC@SECRETSOFTHEARCHMAGES@LORDS@WALBURGIS_RACE@BIO"
msgstr "The antisaint of all forsaken souls, who is whispered to govern the power to undo misfortune, illness, and even old age. In darkness and in shame, Walburgis is the last refuge of many shunned and forgotten mortals who desperately summon him into their hearts each night, even though he is foul and his fruits are rotten. [br/][br/]The Bloodgurgler Legion is believed to be the physical manifestation of the [hyperlink,GLOBAL.DemonicOverlordLoreConcept]Great Bloodgurgler[/hyperlink], who moves through the spirits of his foul and filthy children. To eat the sickly and the elderly and gurgle up their rotten ichor whenever they bleat out in relish, or in their hideous warcries."

msgid "DLC@SECRETSOFTHEARCHMAGES@LORDS@YSARIEL@NAME"
msgstr "Ysariel^M"

msgid "DLC@SECRETSOFTHEARCHMAGES@LORDS@YSARIEL@SECONDNAME"
msgstr "Arbiter of Obbadoth^z"

msgid "DLC@SECRETSOFTHEARCHMAGES@LORDS@YSARIEL@TITLE"
msgstr "Fallen Archon"

msgid "DLC@SECRETSOFTHEARCHMAGES@LORDS@YSARIEL@TITLE@GENDER"
msgstr "^m"

msgid "DLC@SECRETSOFTHEARCHMAGES@LORDS@YSARIEL_CITY_NAME"
msgstr "Throne of Azh'Ruun^N"

msgid "DLC@SECRETSOFTHEARCHMAGES@LORDS@YSARIEL_CITY_NAME_00"
msgstr "Emnora's Umbrage^N"

msgid "DLC@SECRETSOFTHEARCHMAGES@LORDS@YSARIEL_CITY_NAME_01"
msgstr "Fiendscar Basilica^N"

msgid "DLC@SECRETSOFTHEARCHMAGES@LORDS@YSARIEL_CITY_NAME_02"
msgstr "Penitent Bulwark^N"

msgid "DLC@SECRETSOFTHEARCHMAGES@LORDS@YSARIEL_CITY_NAME_03"
msgstr "Buffeted Monastery^N"

msgid "DLC@SECRETSOFTHEARCHMAGES@LORDS@YSARIEL_RAC@NAME"
msgstr "Brotherhood of Ysariel"

msgid "DLC@SECRETSOFTHEARCHMAGES@LORDS@YSARIEL_RACE@BIO"
msgstr "He who smote {GLOBAL.ObbadothLoreConcept.Hyperlink} into submission. Ysariel, son of [hyperlink,GLOBAL.MalielLoreConcept]Maliel[/hyperlink], a lonesome, \"fallen [hyperlink,GLOBAL.ArchonsLoreConcept]Archon[/hyperlink]\" who, after countless failed attempts, eventually established the infamous [hyperlink,GLOBAL.CircleOfDeogaiLoreConcept]Circle of the Azh'Ruun Pit[/hyperlink] through an illicit pact—after which he was banished from Emnora. Now, abandoned by his own and twisted through millennia of forsaken servitude, Ysariel has become the only thing standing between the {GLOBAL.AstralSeaLoreConcept.Hyperlink} and the raging [hyperlink,GLOBAL.DemonicOverlordLoreConcept]Demon Overlords[/hyperlink], bound below the Pit. [br/][br/]In this mission, he stands united with the Brotherhood of Ysariel, his sworn Pact Brothers and Sisters, who stand by his side, forever. As does he, by theirs—through fire and temptation."

msgid "DLC@SECRETSOFTHEARCHMAGES@MEGAWONDERS_STRATEGIC@BROKEN_WIZARD_TOWER@DESCRIPTION"
msgstr "<<m:{GLOBAL.ProvinceConcept.Hyperlink}>> adjacent to this Landmark gain:[bulletlist][bullet/]{knowledgebonus} {GLOBAL.KnowledgeConcept.Hyperlink}.[bullet/]A {GLOBAL.ResearchPostConcept.Hyperlink} in the Province gains {manabonus} {GLOBAL.ManaConcept.Hyperlink} income.[bullet/]The {GLOBAL.PROPERTIES.ELEMENTAL_DEFENSES.Hyperlink} {GLOBAL.CombatEnchantmentConcept.Hyperlink}.[/bulletlist][br/]A {GLOBAL.CityConcept.Hyperlink} with {amount} <<m:{GLOBAL.ProvinceConcept.Hyperlink}>> adjacent to this Landmark gains:[bulletlist][bullet/]Enemy <<m:{GLOBAL.SpellConcept.Hyperlink}>> have {percentage} chance of {GLOBAL.BackfireConcept.Hyperlink} within the domain.[bullet/]The City's owner gains {castingpoints} <<m:{GLOBAL.WorldMapCastingPointConcept.Hyperlink}>> and <<m:{GLOBAL.CombatCastingPointConcept.Hyperlink}>>.[bullet/]Unlocks the {GLOBAL.SPECIAL_OPERATIONS.BROKEN_WIZARD_TOWER_SPELL.Hyperlink} {GLOBAL.CitySpellConcept.Hyperlink}.[/bulletlist]"

msgid "DLC@SECRETSOFTHEARCHMAGES@MEGAWONDERS_STRATEGIC@BROKEN_WIZARD_TOWER@LORE"
msgstr "\"Imagine the masters of strongly opposing magics all gathered within a single tower. They may hate each other to oblivion, but they have learned to respect that every affinity must seep through a world for it to be in equilibrium. The Wizard's Throne is the ultimate guarantor of a [hyperlink,GLOBAL.CircleOfDeogaiLoreConcept]Circle of Deogai's[/hyperlink] balance. For it reminds all Wizards of their own diminutiveness within the vast schemes of the cosmos.\"[br/][br/]— Gabriel, Chronicles of Evermore"

msgid "DLC@SECRETSOFTHEARCHMAGES@MEGAWONDERS_STRATEGIC@BROKEN_WIZARD_TOWER@NAME"
msgstr "Broken Wizard's Throne"

msgid "DLC@SECRETSOFTHEARCHMAGES@MEGAWONDERS_STRATEGIC@BROKEN_WIZARD_TOWER@SPELL@DESCRIPTION"
msgstr "[bulletlist][bullet/]Requires target owned {GLOBAL.CityConcept.Hyperlink} with {amount} or more <<m:{GLOBAL.ProvinceConcept.Hyperlink}>> in its {GLOBAL.DomainConcept.Hyperlink} adjacent to the {GLOBAL.STRUCTURES.BROKEN_WIZARD_TOWER.Hyperlink}.[bullet/]Each City can only be targeted once by this Spell.[bullet/]Immediately unlocks a random {GLOBAL.SpellConcept.Hyperlink} that you do not have access to yet.[/bulletlist]"

msgid "DLC@SECRETSOFTHEARCHMAGES@MEGAWONDERS_STRATEGIC@BROKEN_WIZARD_TOWER@SPELL@NAME"
msgstr "Cosmic Inspiration"

msgid "DLC@SECRETSOFTHEARCHMAGES@MEGAWONDERS_STRATEGIC@CHAINED_DEMON@DESCRIPTION"
msgstr "<<m:{GLOBAL.ProvinceConcept.Hyperlink}>> adjacent to this Landmark gain:[bulletlist][bullet/]{manabonus} {GLOBAL.ManaConcept.Hyperlink} and {draftbonus} {GLOBAL.UnitProductionConcept.Hyperlink}.[bullet/]The {GLOBAL.PROPERTIES.SCORCHING_STENCH_OF_SUFFERING.Hyperlink} {GLOBAL.CombatEnchantmentConcept.Hyperlink}.[/bulletlist][br/]A {GLOBAL.CityConcept.Hyperlink} with {amount} <<m:{GLOBAL.ProvinceConcept.Hyperlink}>> adjacent to this Landmark gains:[bulletlist][bullet/]{manabonus2} {GLOBAL.ManaConcept.Hyperlink} and {draftbonus2} {GLOBAL.UnitProductionConcept.Hyperlink} per Province with {GLOBAL.ChasmConcept.Hyperlink} or {GLOBAL.LavaConcept.Hyperlink} in the {GLOBAL.DomainConcept.Hyperlink}.[bullet/]The City's owner gains the {GLOBAL.SPECIAL_OPERATIONS.CHAINED_DEMON_SPELL.Hyperlink} {GLOBAL.DebuffSpellConcept.Hyperlink}.[/bulletlist]"

msgid "DLC@SECRETSOFTHEARCHMAGES@MEGAWONDERS_STRATEGIC@CHAINED_DEMON@LORE"
msgstr "Black banners billowed above [hyperlink,GLOBAL.ObbadothLoreConcept]The Carnage Bounds[/hyperlink].[br/]Hellions held hard; their titan-lords roared.[br/]Yet hosts of [hyperlink,GLOBAL.DemonicOverlordLoreConcept]The Nether Prime[/hyperlink] came clawing skyward fiercely, while [hyperlink,GLOBAL.YsarielLoreConcept]The Future Throne[/hyperlink] broke gates and bulwark.[br/]Thus Demon-kind surged forth; the elder breed perished.[br/][br/]—Liztia Great Skald of Pseumodius, Victory Poem of the Hellion Wars"

msgid "DLC@SECRETSOFTHEARCHMAGES@MEGAWONDERS_STRATEGIC@CHAINED_DEMON@NAME"
msgstr "Perishing Archnemesis"

msgid "DLC@SECRETSOFTHEARCHMAGES@MEGAWONDERS_STRATEGIC@CHAINED_DEMON@SPELL@DESCRIPTION"
msgstr "Target enemy {GLOBAL.UnitConcept}:[bulletlist][bullet/]Has {percentage} chance of suffering {GLOBAL.PROPERTIES.BURNING.Hyperlink} for {turn} <<m:{GLOBAL.TurnConcept.Hyperlink}>>.[bulletlist][bullet/]This effect repeats {times} times.[/bulletlist][bullet/]Suffers {GLOBAL.PROPERTIES.IMMOBILIZED.Hyperlink} and {GLOBAL.PROPERTIES.PACIFIED.Hyperlink} for {turn2} {GLOBAL.TurnConcept.Hyperlink}.[/bulletlist]"

msgid "DLC@SECRETSOFTHEARCHMAGES@MEGAWONDERS_STRATEGIC@CHAINED_DEMON@SPELL@NAME"
msgstr "Brimstone Bind"

msgid "DLC@SECRETSOFTHEARCHMAGES@MEGAWONDERS_STRATEGIC@CHAINED_DEMON_RMG@NAME"
msgstr "Chained Hellion"

msgid "DLC@SECRETSOFTHEARCHMAGES@MEGAWONDERS_STRATEGIC@CHAINED_HELLION@LORE"
msgstr "\"I can hear them screaming; beasts of chaos incarnated, subdued and bound in chains. They howl in rage and pain, swearing to destroy those who confined them. They tell their story again and again, so they never forget the hatred that keeps them alive. Oh... how I wish I could hunt them again.\" [br/][br/]— Demonic Prince Karavar, The Hellion Wars."

msgid "DLC@SECRETSOFTHEARCHMAGES@MEGAWONDERS_STRATEGIC@ELDRITCH_LURE@NAME"
msgstr "Eldritch Lure"

msgid "DLC@SECRETSOFTHEARCHMAGES@MEGAWONDERS_STRATEGIC@ELDRITCH_LURE@PROPERTY_DESCRIPTION"
msgstr "This unit is inside a {GLOBAL.ProvinceConcept.Hyperlink} with or adjacent to the {GLOBAL.STRUCTURES.LEVIATHAN_TENTACLES.Hyperlink} and therefore:[bulletlist][bullet/]Suffers {GLOBAL.PROPERTIES.DISTRACTED.Hyperlink}.[bullet/]Cannot regenerate and loses {hp} <<m:{GLOBAL.HitPointConcept.Hyperlink}>> per {GLOBAL.TurnConcept.Hyperlink}.[/bulletlist]"

msgid "DLC@SECRETSOFTHEARCHMAGES@MEGAWONDERS_STRATEGIC@LEVIATHAN_PART@NAME"
msgstr "Leviathan Landmark"

msgid "DLC@SECRETSOFTHEARCHMAGES@MEGAWONDERS_STRATEGIC@LEVIATHAN_PARTS@LORE"
msgstr "\"First, it brought the night. The light was eclipsed by its gargantuan shape, still veiled behind the overcast sky. Tentacles pierced the clouds, heralding the arrival of the beast. And then it fell. There was no sky—only the Leviathan. And its grotesque body, plunging like the end of all things.\"[br/][br/]— Sumuskira the Grovetender, Tales of the Elder: As cited by Reskar Scapeshaper"

msgid "DLC@SECRETSOFTHEARCHMAGES@MEGAWONDERS_STRATEGIC@LEVIATHAN_PART_01@DESCRIPTION"
msgstr "<<m:{GLOBAL.ProvinceConcept.Hyperlink}>> adjacent to this Landmark gain:[bulletlist][bullet/]{IntHappinessPenalty} {GLOBAL.CityStabilityConcept.Hyperlink} and {IntKnowledgeBonus} {GLOBAL.KnowledgeConcept.Hyperlink}.[bullet/]The {combatenchantment} {GLOBAL.CombatEnchantmentConcept.Hyperlink}.[/bulletlist][br/]A {GLOBAL.CityConcept.Hyperlink} with {amount} <<m:{GLOBAL.ProvinceConcept.Hyperlink}>> adjacent to this Landmark gains:[bulletlist][bullet/]{IntKnowledgeBonus2} {GLOBAL.KnowledgeConcept.Hyperlink}[bullet/]Allows recruitment of <<m:{GLOBAL.UNITS.ASTRAL_WISP_UNIT.Hyperlink}>>, <<m:{GLOBAL.UNITS.ASTRAL_SERPENT_UNIT.Hyperlink}>>, and <<m:{GLOBAL.UNITS.ASTRAL_SIPHONER_UNIT.Hyperlink}>>.[bullet/]On new round this Landmark is bound, putting it in a dormant state where its other adjacency effects are disabled.[/bulletlist]"

msgid "DLC@SECRETSOFTHEARCHMAGES@MEGAWONDERS_STRATEGIC@LEVIATHAN_PART_01@NAME"
msgstr "Leviathan Eyes^p"

msgid "DLC@SECRETSOFTHEARCHMAGES@MEGAWONDERS_STRATEGIC@LEVIATHAN_PART_02@NAME"
